  "term": "abreaction",
  "definition": "Abreaction is a psychotherapy process in which a person becomes less sensitive to emotionally painful memories, often ones that have been forgotten or repressed, by bringing them back to mind and expressing their reactions to them in a safe therapeutic setting.",
